|~ `::fail`, the step `!|` runs on an error alone, and what is declared
   under it: its constructor and its refusals.
   The rules it holds: [QSDSP#residence]. ~|

:fail
  |~~ The fail track, `a !| b`: the step `b` runs on a failure alone,
      caught to its error at rest, and any other value passes it by, so
      it is where a failure is read, recovered or raised again, while
      `|` passes a failure by. `"x" | add 1 !| 0` answers `0`.

      In a quote the step is a record that holds the quote of the step it
      stands for, `~(!| get /kind) | first` answering `::fail~(get /kind)`.
      ::link~(::error) ::link~(::qlang/errors)
  ~~|
  ::kind
    | accepts |~~ The quote of a step, built into the step `!| step`. ~~| ::quote
    | throws :PayloadKindNotTakenError
        |~~ The payload of `::fail` is the quote of the step it stands for, so
            `~(get /kind) | tag ::fail` is the step `!| get /kind`.
            ::link~(::fail)
        ~~|
    | throws :PayloadNotOneStepError
        |~~ The quote `::fail` holds is one step, the step `!|` runs, and
            no step of the fail track: a pipeline under `!|` is written as
            a group, `~((get /kind | print)) | tag ::fail` the step
            `!| (get /kind | print)`.
            ::link~(::fail)
        ~~|
    | throws :StepNotCommandError
        |~~ A value after `!|` is the recovery the catch answers, but for a
            path, which the verb that takes it reads: `:message` names that
            verb, `get`.
            ::link~(::fail) ::link~(::qlang/pipeline)
        ~~|
        ~(wires :message |~~ What the rule says of the path, the verb that takes it. ~~| ::string
          | wires :found |~~ The value written after `!|`. ~~|)
    | proves :holdsItsStep
        |~~ The fail track holds its step as a quote. ~~|
        ~(~(!| get /kind) | first | payload | eq ~(get /kind))
    | proves :PayloadKindNotTakenError/refusesANumber
        |~~ A number payload is refused. ~~|
        ~(42 | tag ::fail !| get [tag (found | tag)] | eq [::fail/PayloadKindNotTakenError ::number])
    | proves :PayloadKindNotTakenError/buildsTheStepOfAStep
        |~~ The quote of a step builds the step the fail track runs. ~~|
        ~(~(get /kind) | tag ::fail | get [it] | tag ::quote | eq ~(!| get /kind))
    | proves :PayloadNotOneStepError/refusesAPipelineOutsideAGroup
        |~~ A pipeline the fail track holds without a group is refused. ~~|
        ~(~(a | b) | tag ::fail !| tag | eq ::fail/PayloadNotOneStepError)
    | proves :PayloadNotOneStepError/refusesAnEmptyQuote
        |~~ An empty quote holds no step to run. ~~|
        ~(~() | tag ::fail !| tag | eq ::fail/PayloadNotOneStepError)
    | proves :PayloadNotOneStepError/refusesAStepOfTheFailTrack
        |~~ A step of the fail track is no step the fail track runs. ~~|
        ~(~(!| get /kind) | tag ::fail !| tag | eq ::fail/PayloadNotOneStepError)
    | proves :PayloadNotOneStepError/holdsAPipelineInAGroup
        |~~ A pipeline in a group is the one step the fail track runs. ~~|
        ~(~((get /kind | print)) | tag ::fail | get [it] | tag ::quote | eq ~(!| (get /kind | print)))
    | proves :StepNotCommandError/refusesAPath
        |~~ A path after `!|` is refused, naming the verb that reads it. ~~|
        ~([/kind] | tag ::quote | tag ::fail !| get [tag message] | eq [::fail/StepNotCommandError "a path is a value, which the verb that takes it reads: write `get /kind`"])
    | impl ::builtin{};

